@meeting promo.officer
// Pillar 5 Step 3, the first promotion (Day 10, Wednesday, 11:00): Calder's glass office in the Works bay, after the
// summons. She tells you you've passed, gives you the Technician's badge and the Officer's collar pip; one reply, which
// she remembers (C2 stores promo.reply 1-3 by the choices' order: proud, surprised, about time; keep it). If she had to come and find you (11:15), the same script
// plays where you are. Seat C2 plays it. Head writer W2.
title: My office, 11:00
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder promoted you to Officer: Technician, Tier 2. A badge, a collar pip, and your own cabin from tonight.
== lines
calder > you: Sit. No, stay standing. This won't take long.   [gesture]
calder: The scrubber. Filter in, fan settled, nobody had to tell you twice.
calder: You've passed. As of now you're an Officer. Technician, Tier 2.
calder: The badge. And the pip. Collar, left side. Straight, please.
? choice
* Thank you, Chief. I won't let you down.   rel:calder+2
  calder: I know. That's why you're standing here.   [nod]
* Me? Already?   rel:calder+1
  calder: Already. I don't promote people to be kind. I promote them because they're ready.
* About time, honestly.   rel:calder+1
  calder: Hm. Torres said you'd say that. He owes me a biscuit.   [laugh]
calder: The board leaves you Tier 2 work from tomorrow. Harder faults. Fewer carts.
calder: Tonight you move to 4-23. Your own cabin. I'll walk you there at five.
calder: The Captain commissions you tomorrow. Clean uniform. Go on, then. They're waiting outside.
